---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Camera monitoring options | OurPort" description="Plan optional camera monitoring around the OurPort laundry handoff, property policy, coverage, ownership and retention requirements.">
  <section class="container option-hero">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Optional site extension · CCTV</p><h1>Visibility around <span>the handoff.</span></h1><p class="lead">A camera can help document approach and open-door events. Whether it belongs to the property or an OurPort monitoring arrangement is decided before installation.</p><a class="button" href="/plan-a-site/?role=housing">Discuss your site <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    <figure><img src="/images/cctv-monitoring-concept.jpg" width="1370" height="1151" alt="Illustrative OurPort locker with a small dome camera mounted beneath its illuminated header." fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption><span>Locker-mounted camera concept</span><span>Illustrative · configuration not final</span></figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <section class="section option-tint option-tint-blue"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Three paths to review</p><h2>Fit monitoring to the property.</h2></div><p>A camera is an option, not a default promise. The property’s security team and policies determine the appropriate path.</p></div><div class="option-paths"><article><span>01</span><h3>Use property CCTV</h3><p>Position the handoff within approved coverage and keep video authority with the existing property platform.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Add a locker camera</h3><p>Review a suitable PoE camera, view, mounting point and integration path with the property before specifying it.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Proceed without video</h3><p>Where monitoring is unnecessary or not approved, use access and door-event records within the agreed operating model.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section container option-decisions"><div><p class="eyebrow">Before a camera is selected</p><h2>Six decisions establish the boundary.</h2></div><ol><li><span>01</span>What area may be viewed</li><li><span>02</span>Who owns and administers the video</li><li><span>03</span>Which network and VMS are approved</li><li><span>04</span>How long recordings are retained</li><li><span>05</span>Who may request or review footage</li><li><span>06</span>How signage, privacy and incidents are handled</li></ol></section>
  <section class="section option-diagram"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Ownership before equipment</p><h2>Keep video governance explicit.</h2></div><p>The working concept prefers the property’s existing video-management system. Any separate monitoring service requires its own written scope.</p></div><figure><img src="/images/data-power-governance-flow.png" width="1872" height="1216" alt="Concept diagram separating locker power, network and camera-video ownership paths." loading="lazy" /><figcaption><span>Data, power and governance concept</span><span>For coordination only · engineering validation required</span></figcaption></figure></div></section>
  <section class="container sibling-option"><div><p class="eyebrow">Related option</p><h2>Plan the network path with it.</h2><p>Camera, controls and notifications depend on an approved connection. Review Ethernet and WAP options alongside monitoring.</p></div><a class="button button-outline" href="/wifi-wap/">Explore WiFi & WAP options <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
  <CallToAction role="housing" title="Define the monitoring boundary first." body="Tell us about the site, its existing CCTV platform and the people responsible for security and network approval." />
</SiteLayout>
